icleshow/128276173.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/etimes/trending/doj-files-reveal-exactly-how-jeffrey-epstein-makes-his-coffee-full-step-by-step-guide-inside/articleshow/128276173.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-02-13T05:57:12+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Trending Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-128282271,imgsize-1423449.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Water and oxygen aren’t enough: Scientists reveal two ‘must-have’ ingredients for life on other planets]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/128272637.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[New research from ETH Zurich challenges the long-held “follow the water” rule in the search for extraterrestrial life. Scientists argue that a planet’s habitability depends on a narrow chemical balance during core formation, preserving phosphorus and nitrogen in its mantle. Earth falls within this rare “Goldilocks” range, potentially making truly life-supporting worlds far rarer than assumed.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/water-and-oxygen-arent-enough-scientists-reveal-two-must-have-ingredients-for-life-on-other-planets/articleshow/128272637.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/water-and-oxygen-arent-enough-scientists-reveal-two-must-have-ingredients-for-life-on-other-planets/articleshow/128272637.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-02-13T02:23:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-128275706,imgsize-43436.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Republican slams Purdue University for hiring H-1B worker for $149,000 software engineer role]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" sty